> Conclusion

The shortcut adds a direct path, while post-add ReLU still gates signed signals. Projection
shortcuts change both sampling and channel count. The canonical checks and the compact fits make those details visible.
The saved moving moments are part of each selected checkpoint.

> References

- [He et al. (2016), Deep Residual Learning for Image Recognition](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03385).
- [Authors' ResNet-50 topology](https://github.com/KaimingHe/deep-residual-networks/blob/master/prototxt/ResNet-50-deploy.prototxt).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
